1 CONT Joseph B. Johns settled in Tennessee in 1801.  He lived briefly in Giles C o.,
1 CONT TN and then settled in Rutherford Co., TN.  He served in the War of 1812.
1 CONT He enlisted 10 Dec 1812 and served as a private Captain Newtons Co., Col.
1 CONT Wm. Halls Regiment of West TN Militia 12-10-1812; and private in Capt.
1 CONT Nathan Davis' Co. in Regt. under Gen. Andrew Jackson, 12-18-1813.
1 CONT He purchased  land on E. Fork Stones Riiver and at his death owned
1 CONT about 1,000 acres.
1 CONT
1 CONT This grave site is located on private property. There are 3 stones.
1 CONT One without engraving is broken in many pieces.  The two with the
1 CONT inscription are broken from their base but the inscription part is
1 CONT intact. They were laying on the ground covered by weeds.  They are
1 CONT currently leaning against a fence. It is incorrectly listed in several
1 CONT publications as being west of Walter Hill on 266.  The descriptions
1 CONT incorrectly put it on property that was owned by my grandfather Will
1 CONT Boone Johns.  With the help of Ernest King Johns and my uncle Hascal
1 CONT Johns I was able to locate the site of the graves off 266 East.
1 CONT Traveling from Murfreesboro, TN on 231 No.  Travel about 10 miles
1 CONT to the intersection of 231 and 266 at the Walter Hill intersection.
1 CONT Take a right onto 266 East towards Lascassas.  Travel 2.1 miles to
1 CONT Dunnaway Chapel Rd.(Kings Chapel Baptist Chruch).  Take a left and
1 CONT travel 1.3 miles to Lane Rd.  Take a left on Lane Rd. and travel
1 CONT .06 mile to bridge over creek.  The graves are located approx. 300-400 yd s. N.W. in the corner of a fence line behind the old home.  The land was o wned by a Johns descendant until the 1960s when it was sold to Jack Lan e.  There is a new brick h
1 CONC ome built on the property and the old house is s cheduled to be torn down
1 CONT spring 2001.  Standing at the bridge looking toward the new home the gra ve sites are approx 100 yds. to the right.
1 CONT
1 CONT Many thanks to Estelle Hall for providing the records in Rutherford Count y, TN for Joseph B. Johns.
1 CONT
1 CONT The middle name of Joseph B. Johns:
1 CONT
1 CONT Many Johns researchers, among them Edythe Rucker Whitley, believed that t he middle name of Joseph B. Johns was Barksdale.  This was an easy assumpt ion to make, as Joseph B. Johns had a son who was named Joseph Barksdale J ohns.  However, the Bar
1 CONC ksdale name was first introduced into the Johns fam ily by Elizabeth Vaughan, wife of Joseph B. Johns.  There is no connecti on in the lineage of Joseph B. Johns with the Barksdale family and absolut ely no reason that his middle name would have b
1 CONC een Barksdale.
1 CONT
1 CONT It is likely that his middle name was "BENJAMIN" as General Joseph Benjam in Palmer, grandson of Joseph B. Johns and Elizabeth Vaughan, was pro ud of the fact that he was named for his grandfather Johns.  Althou gh it is also possible that his mid
1 CONC dle name may have been Benning.
1 CONT
