1 CONC IGI gives dob: Abt. 1752,  Frederick Co. Virginia; another IGI source gives Abt. 1754, but also lists Fredeick, Co.
1 CONT Bill Jobe gives dod as 1826.  He also gives his name as "Colonel" Jeremiah McKay.  Is this honorary or did he serve in the Revolutionary War?  He would have been of age to do so.-LKL
1 CONT December 28, 1790  Jeremiah McKay of Shenandoah County, Virginia, gave a power of attorney to his well beloved friends, David Job of Washington County and Abraham McKay of Green County, both of North Carolina, to act respecting the settlement an
1 CONC d receiving of his wife's part of the estate of Joseph Whitson, deceased, to have, use, and take all lawful means to his power for the recovery of sums of money and acquittances. -- Jobe's Journal
1 CONT
