1 CONC "Dr. Zach's daughter, Emily Virginia, was his oldest child still at home when the [Civil] War started.  She was 21 years old when the hostilities began.  She was of great help to her father and mother, and assisted Dr. Zach in his care of the woun
1 CONC ded.  She fell in love with a handsome wounded Yankee from Boston.  In a matter of days they became engaged.  But his wounds were fatal and he died.  Madeline Johnson remembered that Dr. Zach's family felt that 'People from Boston are more like th
1 CONC e Virginia folks'" -- From The War Years at Milford by F.B. Compton
1 CONT
