1 CONC [johns file.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT THOMAS JOHNS was the son of William Johns and his wife Ann. Ann's maiden n ame is believed to have been Merryman.  THOMAS JOHNS' daughter, Elizabe th Merriman Johns, was one of a number of the descendants of William and A nn Johns of Buckingham Co
1 CONC unty whose surname, or middle name, was Merryman/ Merriman.
1 CONT
1 CONT Descendants of THOMAS JOHNS, please be aware that incorrect information w as published about THOMAS JOHNS of Pittsylvania County, VA by Edythe Ruck er Whitley.  He was not, as she claimed, the son of John Johns who di ed in 1778 in Charlotte Count
1 CONC y, VA.  John Johns of Charlotte County h ad a son by the name of Thomas Johns, but he was not THOMAS JOHNS of Pitts ylvania County, VA.  Thomas Johns, son of John Johns of Charlotte Count y, lived in Charlotte County until his death in 1847.  He w
1 CONC as married to F rances "Frankie" Claybrook and the father of at least five children, all b orn in Charlotte County.
1 CONT
1 CONT THOMAS JOHNS military record from the Revolutionary War place him in Bucki ngham County, VA.
1 CONT
1 CONT THOMAS JOHNS was living in Pittsylvania County, VA by 1784 when he purchas ed land from John Stockton 17 May 1784 (Deed Book 7, pg. 273, Pittsylvan ia Co., VA).  He also purchased land on Pigg River from James Karr 16 S ep 1787 (Deed Book 8, pg 94
1 CONC , Pittsylvania Co., VA).
1 CONT
1 CONT Land patent for THOMAS JOHNS:
1 CONT
1 CONT 19 Jul 1790- THOMAS JOHNS Pittsylvania County, 160 acres on the north si de of Pig River adjoining land of Adkinson, King, Peak and others. Gran ts 22, p. 409.
1 CONT
1 CONT THOMAS JOHNS served in the Revolutionary War.  He was an Ensign in the Buc kingham County Militia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Richmond, Virginia State Archives, 10 April 1784. Reference Auditor's Acco unt XVIII, page 531, Militia Warrant to Thomas Johns for his service in t he militia of the state in 1781.
1 CONT
1 CONT RECORDS PERTAINING TO THE DIVISION OF THE ESTATE OF THOMAS JOHNS:
1 CONT
1 CONT 30 Dec 1794- In obedience to an order of the Worshipfull Court of Pittsylv ania Co. we Robret Devin, Joseph Austin and Abraham Aaron, to take an inve ntory and appraisement of the estate of THOMAS JOHNS, decd. We do hereby c ertify that we have ap
1 CONC praised the foregoing articles (named) and find th at same to amount to the sum of 800 pounds.
1 CONT Signed: Robert Devin, Joseph Austin and Abram Aaron.
1 CONT
1 CONT At a Court held of Pittsylvania County, VA the 19th day of January 1796 t he above inventory was returned and the same was ordered to be record ed by the court. Teste: Wm. Tunstall.
1 CONT (Pittsylvania Co., VA, Will Book 2, pg. 186)
1 CONT
1 CONT 20 Dec 1800- In obedience to an order of the Worshipfull Court of Pittsylv ania County we have proceeded to divide the estate of THOMAS JOHNS, decd ., among the dependent legatees in manner and form to wit:
1 CONT
1 CONT Lot 1: To Isaac Johns: Jame and Rhoda valued at $118.00
1 CONT
1 CONT Lot 2: To Judith Johns: Charles, Ralph and Mary valued at $112.00.
1 CONT
1 CONT Lot 3. To Elizabeth Johns: Nancy, Charity and Joseph valued at $135.00.
1 CONT
1 CONT Lot 4. To Polly Johns: Cuzzy, Polly and Lucy valued at $114.00
1 CONT
1 CONT Lot 5. To Jacob Johns: Jessey and Ann valued at $105.00
1 CONT
1 CONT Lot 6. To Joseph Johns: Alley and Elijah valued at $115.00
1 CONT
1 CONT Lot 7. To Abraham Johns: Phebe, Reubin, Stephen and Usley valued at $130.0 0.
1 CONT
1 CONT Given under our hands this day above written.
1 CONT Signed: James Blakely, Joseph Austin and Abraham Aaron.
1 CONT (Pittsylvania Co., VA, Will Book 3, pg. 95)
1 CONT
1 CONT From: Mixed Probate Records - Pittsylvania County, VA
1 CONT Book 4, 1805 -1812
1 CONT
1 CONT Johns, Thomas  - Charles Lewis & Gatreyhood his wife, adms.
1 CONT Names: Abraham, Elizabeth, Isaac, Jacob, Judith, Polley & Jos.
