1 CONC "Harvey Triplett
1 CONT "Funeral services for Harvey Franklin Triplett, 82, 118 E. Dryden St., Palmyra, were held at 2 p.m. on Tuesday, June 18 at the First Baptist Church.  The Rev Ben Early officiated and entombment was in the Palmyra Mausoleum.  Lewis Brothers Funera
1 CONC l Home was in charge of arrangements.
1 CONT "Casket bearers were Raymond Pennewell, Randles Summers, Archie Pugh, Will Porter, Otis Miller, and Alva Vaughn
1 CONT "Mr Triplett died at 10:55 p.m. on Saturday, June 15, at Levering Hospital, Hannibal.
1 CONT "He was born on April 7, 1892 in Marion County a son of Jefferson D. Triplett and Jessie Brown Triplett.  He married Sarah Reber in 1919 and she died in 1966.  In 1967 he married Winifred Reighley and she survives.
1 CONT "Mr Triplett was a retired farmer and a member of the First Baptist Church.
1 CONT "Other survivors include two daughters, Mrs James (Jessie Lou) Johnson, Ewing, and Mrs. LaVerne (Dorothy) Robbins, La Prairie, Ill.; one brother, Warwick Triplett, Hannibal; two sisters, Mrs Lula Carson, Quincy, Ill. and Mrs Joe Atwater, St. Charl
1 CONC es; six grandchildren and three great-grandchildren.
1 CONT "He was preceded in death by one brother." -- Palmyra Spectator
1 CONT
