1 CONT He was believed to be the youngest son of Baron Otto Van Tuyl and his wife Neeltje.  On April 16, 1663,  he sailed from Holland to Bedford, Long Island in "De Bonte Koe" (The Spotted Cow)  with his wife and child two years old.  He settled in NY
1 CONC C along by the "Wall." -- From: "Van Tuyl Ancestry of Mary Ellenor Stafford Bowman,"  p. xviii. from un-noted printed source.
