1 CONC "Both Edward and Mary Jane Mallory were born in Frederick County, Virginia, and emigrated to Missouri.  According to the 'Portrait and Biographical Record,' Edward ' was a life-long member of the Methodist Church, but his wife was a Baptist.  Duri
1 CONC ng the war his sympathies were with the Union and in politics he used his franchise in favor of the Democratic party.  At the close of a good and useful life he was summoned to his reward, December 14, 1881.  For thirty years he was engaged in wor
1 CONC king at the carpenter's trade and helped build the lock gates on the O.&C. Canal prior to coming west.'
1 CONT "One can imagine the controversy and heartache brought about by the Civil War, as members of the same family held different beliefs.  Although Edward favored the Union, his son, John W. Mallory fought on the side of the South." -- Bond, Marian Sau
1 CONC nders.  Some ancestors, pp. 48-49.
