1 CONT "Shelbina Mo., Dec. 8 -- Funeral services for Mrs Mary Jane White, 89, a pioneer resident of Marion and Shelby counties, who died in the home of her daugher, Mrs Anne Young in Shelbina Thursday morning at 5:30 o'clock were held Saturday in the She
1 CONC lbina Baptist church with burial in the Shelbina cemetery.
1 CONT "Mrs White was born in Schuyler county Missouri, July 2, 1842, the daugher of simon and Anna White [source is incorrect: Simon and Anna Painter Carson] who came to Missouri from Virginia in 1820.  She was married to Lafayette White in 1859.  Mr Wh
1 CONC ite died in 1923  Two children also preceded their mother in death. Edgar W. died in 1915 and Mrs Clara Davis died in 1910.
1 CONT "Surviving are the following children: Mrs Annie Young and Mrs Estella Moore of Shelbina; Mrs Ethat Patterson of Quincy; Simon P. White of Los Angeles; Frank R. White of Lakenan; Thomas B. White of Stoutsville; Linn P. White of Nrookfield and Harv
1 CONC ey C. White of Rock Island.  Eighteen grandchildren and twenty-one great-greandchildren also survive together with a sister Mrs. Leathy Swisher of Cherry Dell, Marion county, Missouri.  Two sisters, Mrs. Amanda Sibbly and Mrs Mattie McLeod and a b
1 CONC rother, John R. Carson, all of Marion county died several years ago.
1 CONT "Mrs White was a member of the Shelbina Baptist church and taught a class in the Sunday school for many years.  Prior to moving to Shelbina she was a member of the Bethel Baptist Church.
