1 CONT July 20, 1956 letter from Hunter B. McKay to Joshua Booten Taylor:
1 CONT "This past spring we came across a very valuable record of the McKay Family in the Virginia Historical Society (See File 415, Abstracts from the Green Collection.)  It seems that a Mr. Thomas Green, an attorney, was interested, in 1823, in locatin
1 CONC g the heirs of Robert McKay for some legal purposes growing out of the suit of McKay, Hite, Duff, and Green against Lord Fairfax, and drew up at that time a table showing most of the descendants of Robert McKay, including children, grandchildren a
1 CONC nd some great-grandchildren.
1 CONT "This record shows quite clearly that your family and the Comptons are connected with the McKays thru Moses, son of Robert Sr. rather than thru Robert Jr., the son from whom I am descended...."
1 CONT
