1 CONT "Quoting from the Quaker records and the Hopewell Friends History (p. 99) ' 1751, Record of Wm. Reckitt at or near Crooked Run : We had a meeting at Crooked Run, 22 miles South of Hopewell on the first day, the 18 of the 12 mo.  It was a good meet
1 CONC ing.  On the second day we set forward through the woods and over the hills and rocks, crossing several large creeks.  We came in the evening to Moses Mackoy, and had a meeting there next day.  They were an unsettled people, yet assented to trut
1 CONC h ; but were not fully convinced in their minds concerning the sufficiency of it ; having an eye to outward shadows.  I left them in good will.'
