1 CONC I knew Uncle Jewell only long after his retirement and had little contact of the sort to permit me to form any idea of his character.  He died of Parkinson's disease from which he suffered for a long time. -- LKL
1 CONT
1 CONT "Death of Well Known Retired Farmer
1 CONT "John Jewel McLeod, age 80, well known retired farmer, passed away at Levering hospital at 6:30 Sunday evening.  He had been in failing health for the last five years.
1 CONT "Son of John Bell and Martha Carson McLeod, he was born March 4, 1875 on a farm west of Palmyra.
1 CONT "On November 24, 1901 he was married to Maude Hansbrough.  They made their home north of Palmyra where he was engaged in stock and dairy farming.
1 CONT "He united with Bethel Baptist church and was active as a deacon and Sunday school superintendent for a number of years.
1 CONT "Mr. McLeod was respected by all who knew him as a man of high principles.
1 CONT "His wife passed away in 1942 and he came to live in Palmyra where he worked for the Farm Bureau Service company until he retired in 1949.
1 CONT "Surviving are one daughter, Helen McLeod; two brothers, Hugh McLeod of Palmyra and Bob McLeod of Independence, Mo.; four sisters, Mrs. J.B. Taylor of Palmyra, Mrs George Imbler and Miss Mabel McLeod of Kirksville, and Mrs. L.A. Harris of Kalispel
1 CONC l, Mont.
1 CONT "Funeral services were held at the First Baptist church Wednesday morning at 10:30 with the Rev. W.E. Sutterfield, pastor of the First Baptist church in charge.  Mrs F.G. Carlstead was organist and Miss Alpha Jo Sutterfield, vocalist.
1 CONT "Pallbearers were William Hansbrough, Harvey Triplett, Warwick Triplett, George Keller, Randles Summers, and Dudley McPike."
0 @N1202@ NOTE
1 CONC "Mrs Anna T. Taylor
1 CONT "Mrs Anna T. Taylor who resided with her husband and daughter at the family home north of Palmyra, died Sunday April 30, 1933, at 4:50 a.m.  Funeral services were held Monday afternoon at 2:30 o'clock at the Bethel Baptist church, Fabius township
1 CONC , conducted by Rev Harold M. Hunt.  Interment was in Bethel Cemetery.  Pallbearers who served at the ceremony were A. Robbins, Frank Hansbrough, Harvey Triplett, Warwick Triplett, John Hansbrough, and Frank McPike.
1 CONT "Deceased was a daughter of the late J.B. and Martha McLeod and was born March 31, 1873 bringing her to the age of 60 years, 1month and 9 days at the time of her death.  She is survived by her husband, Cecil R. Taylor, one daughter, Miss Mable Mau
1 CONC rine Taylor, at home, five sisters: Mrs Lulu White and Mrs. J.B. Taylor of this county, Mrs. George Imbler and Miss Mabel McLeod of Kirksville, and Mrs L.A. Harris who resides in Montana, and by three brothers, H.M. McLeod and J.J. McLeod of thi
1 CONC s county and Robert McLeod of LaGrange.
1 CONT "She was an excellent woman widely known and beloved in home circle and community."  -- Palmyra Spectator [Article was badly photocopied so some words have been supplied by the transcriber, LKL]
0 @N1203@ NOTE
1 CONC "Golden Wedding Celebration
1 CONT "Mr and Mrs. Robert L. McLeod will celebrate their 50th wedding anniversary with open house at the home of Rev. and Mrs Harold M. Hunt of Independence, Mo., December 27, 1943.
1 CONT Robert L. McLeod and Mary E. Scott grew to young manhood and womanhood in Marion County near Palmyra, and were united in marriage at the home of the bride's parents, Mr. and Mrs John Wilfred Scott, December 27, 1893, with Rev. W.H. Stone of LaGran
1 CONC ge officiating.  Mr. and Mrs. McLeod are parents of three children; Leland S. of Evanston, Ill with the Stewart-Warner Co., of Chicago; Robert Lloyd who lost his life at the age of 20 years by drowning in river at LaGrange, and Martha Elizabeth, w
1 CONC ife of Rev. Harold M. Hunt, pastor of the First Baptist church of Independence.  There are also five grandchildren, Carmeta Ann and Robert Loyd McLeod; and Kathryn, Mary Lee and Jane Ann Hunt.
1 CONT "Mr. and Mrs. McLeod spent the first years of their married life on the farm in Marion County, and Mr. McLeod was carrier on Rural Route No. 1 out of Palmyra for several years, later moving to LaGrange, to educate their children at LaGrange Colleg
1 CONC e from which institution they were all graduated.  They still maintain a home at LaGrange.
1 CONT "Mr. McLeod spent the last 23 years before retiring in 1940 as Assistant Cashier of the Farmers and Merchants Bank of LaGrange.  The McLeods have been making their home the last three years in the home of Rev. and Mrs. Hunt at Independence, Missou
1 CONC ri.
1 CONT "Mr. and Mrs. McLeod are members of prominent pioneer Marion county families.  During their residence in LaGrange they were active in religious and civic affairs." -- Unnamed source, probably the Palmyra Spectator.
1 CONT
1 CONT "Open House For A Couple Married 60 Years.
1 CONT "Sixty years ago Sunday, on December 27, 1893, Mr. and Mrs. R.L. McLeod were married in a home wedding near Palmyra, Mo.  An open house in their honor was held from 3 to 5 p.m. yesterday at the home of a daughter, Mrs. H.M. Hunt 610 W. Truman, whe
1 CONC re they have made their home since 1941.
1 CONT "Hundreds of friends and neighbors, including Mr. and Mrs. Harry Truman and daughter, Margaret, visited the elderly couple during the day.  Mrs. Hunt and the Rev. Hunt of the First Baptist church were assisted by their daughters, Mrs LeRoy Bisel
1 CONC , Miss Jane Ann Hunt, and Miss Mary Lee Hunt.
1 CONT "Also assisting were members of the Women's Missionary Union, Mrs. J.R. Karm, president and Mrs Warren Douglas and Mrs Ed Williams.  Decorations of pink snapdragons and red roses were arranged by Mrs L.H. Kramer.
1 CONT "Mr. and Mrs McLeod formerly lived at La Grange, Mo where both attended La Grange College.  The Rev and Mrs. Hunt also attended that college.  Mr. McLeod owned a grocery store there for about 20 years and was employed with the bank for over 25 yea
1 CONC rs until his retirement in 1941 when they came to Independence.
1 CONT "Besides their daughter, Mrs. Hunt, the couple have a son, Leland, of Pittsburg [sic], Pa.  Another son drowned when he was 20 years old.  They have 5 grandchildren and one great grandchild, Mark Steven Bisel.
1 CONT "Background music during the reception was played by Jane Ann, violinist and Mary Lee, pianist." -- The Independence Examiner.
1 CONT
1 CONT Kay Long remembers seeing other accounts of this event which headlined the fact that the Trumans attended the affair and gave little information about the McLeods!
1 CONT
