1 CONT "Mrs. Annie McLeod died in the Mayfield Sanitarium in St. Louis on Sunday and her remains reached Palmyra Monday evening.  The funeral occurred at Bethel church Tuesday morning and was conducted by Rev. Mr. Stone, the Pastor.  The large concours
1 CONC e in attendance attested the esteem in which she was held while living and the sympathy felt for her bereaved husband and friends not that she is gone.  Her death is a peculiarly sad one and the HERALD can only join with other friends in words o
1 CONC f condolence for the living.
1 CONT "Annie Scott McLeod was born Nov. 7, 1869; united with the church under Bro. Berry in August, 1885, and was baptized by Bro. Dingle; she died April 11th, 1807."  -- Quincy [?] Herald
