1 CONC el where friends may call until time for the services.
1 CONT "Mr McLeod died Tuesday morning, August 2, 1960, at 3:30 a.m. at the Cookson Rest Home in Quincy.  He had been a patient in the home for eleven days. Prior to that he had been hospitalized for a number of weeks, having been in failing health for t
1 CONC he past several months.
