1 CONT
1 CONT WILLIAM JOHNS served as a Captain in the Buckingham Co. Militia during t he Revolutionary War.
1 CONT
1 CONT Published in the Virginia Gazette 17 August 1777 by Anthony Winston:
1 CONT Hungtinowr, June 30, 1777,, FOR SALE, on very reasonable terms, about 1200
1 CONT acres of very rich TOBACCO LAND, on each side Great Ducker's creek, in the
1 CONT lower end of Buckingham county, near Appomattox river.  On this la nd is a well built house having two rooms on a floor, with a porch, necess ary outhouses, and an excellent young orchard.  I really do not know any r icher high ground than is on t
1 CONC his tract.  Also a plantation, with a good o rchard, on each side of Little Willis's creek, and about 1000 acres of go od land.  On both places is great plenty of good meadow land, and fine ran ge for stock.  I believe no place in Virginia is heal
1 CONC thier than hereabouts ----I would rent a place called the New Store, where Capt. JOHNS lives.  T here is a good dwelling house with 5 rooms on the lower floor, a merchant 's house, a storehouse, etc.  It is a very fine place for a store or ordin a
1 CONC ry, lying within sight of where the great Buckingham road joins the Guin ea road, and there are no other roads leading to our extensive back count ry nearer than those by Buckingham and Prince Edward courthouse.
1 CONT
1 CONT Published in the Virginia Gazette 8 July 1777:
1 CONT Last Friday morning the Emerald frigate, lying off our capes, took the
1 CONT following vessels, outward bound, viz. Capt. _ in a small schooner;
1 CONT and the captains Marsh, Philipson, Moodie, and McFee in small sloops. The
1 CONT brig Liberty, capt. Herbert, belonging to this state, and a large sloop Ca pt.
1 CONT JOHNS, both got clear besides a manner of other vessels.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1773-  Buckingham Co. Tax List:  WILLIAM JOHNS, JR. and Hannah, 2 tithes.
1 CONT
