2 TITL Co. E, 35th Bttn. Va. Cav Reunion
2 _DATE 1894
2 _TEXT "This Battalion was commonly called White's Battalion and was commanded by Lt. Col. Elijah V. White an excellent officer and gallant soldier and was frequently in history as "White's Comanches." At first, this reunion was believed to have taken pl
3 CONC ace in 1919, however, an original photo taken by Silas K. Wright in Luray and labeled as such is identical in pose to this photo and indicates that this reunion, more than likely took place in August, 1894. Beginning with the rear rank and continu
3 CONC ing from left to right: George Alva Goyer, William H. Rodgers, Middleton Warfield Yates, George Henderson (Co. B), John Pendleton Grove, Jacob Dallas Slusher, Jacob C. Kibler, Daniel Kemp, Howard Richards (Co. A), James H. Shenk (Co. D, 7th Va. Ca
3 CONC v.), John Robert McCullough, Philip Monroe Kauffman, John W. Grove, James Booton Compton, Joseph C. Ambrose (Co. C), Milton Bowman, Joseph M. Huffman, Franklin Clem, Captain John H. Grabill, Lieutenant Harrison Monroe Strickler, Charles Bailey Fri
3 CONC stoe, Milton N. Rhodes, Isaac Newton Jennings (Co. A & D), Samuel B. Bowman, ____ Hutchinson (Co. A), Andrew Jackson Brumback, Joel Moreland, Samuel C. Golladay, John P. Mauck, _______ Rudaciller, James W. Thomas Warren, William Edwin Grayson, Joh
3 CONC n Henry Flinn, Ira C. Bumgardner, William T. Kibler, _______ Rudaciller.
