2 TITL Belle Grove
2 _DATE 1797
2 _TEXT Belle Grove was a working grain and livestock farm for nearly one hundred years. The plantation house was built in 1797 for Major Isaac Hite and his wife Nelly, sister of President James Madison. Around 1815, Major Hite controlled 7,500 acres of l
3 CONC and with 103 slave workers.  During the Civil War, Belle Grove was a centerpiece for attack and counter-attack in the Battle of Cedar Creek.
